  "text": "British-born Hong Kong artisan Rickie Cheuk is a materials explorer whose practice centres around experimental making and circular design. Working across disciplines, he creates objects using waste materials sourced from a range of industries, reimagining the overlooked or discarded with inventive craftsmanship. Most recently, Rickie salvaged piping and old sinks from the demolition of a residential home, transforming the waste material into chopsticks, merging structure, materiality, and storytelling. For further information on pricing and availability for Rickie’s work, please contact info@goldenearthstudio.co.uk Artworks Chopsticks by Rickie Cheuk Back to Artists Bespoke Commissions Golden Earth Studio offers a bespoke commission service that utilises the construction byproducts of our clients’ homes. To explore the possibilities of commissioning a unique piece of artwork to compliments your interior space, get in touch via our contact form or email. info@goldenearthstudio.co.uk First & Last Name Email Phone Message Send",
